<title>DUBAI: Ship carrying barley runs aground off Saudi coast.</title>
<headline>Ship carrying barley runs aground off Saudi coast.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-02-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>A cargo ship carrying 34,000 tonnes of bulk barley ran aground off the coast of Dammam in eastern Saudi Arabia, the daily Saudi Gazette reported on Saturday.</p>
<p>The ship was about 200 km (120 miles) from the King Abdul-Aziz Seaport in Dammam, the paper said, adding the vessel would be refloated after some of its cargo had been unloaded.</p>
<p>It did not say how the ship ran aground or when the incident had occurred.</p>
